# ── Not for publication ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The repository is meant to be open source. These are the parts that must not be,
# and the reason is different for each one.
#
# l1-snipe/ is the bundled-launch tooling: how the launch transaction and the buys
# are arranged so nobody lands between them. Publishing it publishes the timing to
# anyone who wants to land between them. PROOF-keel.md also names real launch and
# snipe transactions, which ties the technique to specific wallets.
l1-snipe/
#
# miner/ is the optimiser — the client that searches for cheaper bytecode. The whole
# protocol pays for that search. Handing competitors a working one is handing them
# the prize.
miner/
#
# deployments/*.json carry `salt`, and the salt is the single input somebody needs to
# deploy at our predicted token address before we do. Addresses are public and belong
# in the audit package (which strips the salt); this file is written by a deploy and
# is not the place they should be published from.
deployments/*.json
#
# The same-block launch bundle, in the two places it leaks outside l1-snipe/.
# make-launch-sidecar.sh signs an unmined launch and writes the sidecar files the
# bundle needs; LaunchCalldata.s.sol emits the calldata it carries. Either one alone
# is enough to reconstruct the sequencing.
tools/make-launch-sidecar.sh
script/LaunchCalldata.s.sol
